
const STONES={"II.1.01": "A 4-digit number is thousands, hundreds, tens and ones: <math><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>736<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4000<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>700<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>30<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.1.02": "Commas split a number into groups of three: millions, thousands, ones.", "II.1.03": "<math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> shifts every digit one place left; <math><mrow><mo>÷<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> shifts every digit one place right.", "II.1.04": "Compare place by place from the left; the first digit that differs decides.", "II.1.05": "Look at the digit right of the rounding place: 5 or more rounds up; 4 or less rounds down.", "II.1.06": "To round to any place, check the digit to its right, round that place, then fill the rest with zeros.", "II.1.07": "Estimate by rounding each number first; use the estimate to check the exact answer.", "II.1.08": "Line up the places, then add each column from right to left.", "II.1.09": "When a column sums to 10 or more, write its ones digit and carry the rest to the next column.", "II.1.10": "Line up the places, subtract column by column, then check by adding back.", "II.1.11": "If a top digit is too small, trade 1 from the next place left for 10 in this place.", "II.1.12": "Find the whole and the parts: if the whole is missing, add; if a part is missing, subtract.", "II.10.01": "A line plot shows each data value as one mark above a number line.", "II.10.02": "Read each bar's height on the scale; the scale must go up in equal steps.", "II.10.03": "Value <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> number of symbols <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> the key.", "II.10.04": "A frequency table lists each category and how many times it occurs.", "II.10.05": "Mean <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mtext>total<\/mtext><mtext>number of values<\/mtext><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.10.06": "Mode: the most common value. Median: the middle value once the data are in order.", "II.10.07": "Time goes across, the amount goes up; join the points in time order.", "II.10.08": "Question, collect, organize, display, conclude.", "II.10.09": "Read the scale first: where it starts, and how it steps.", "III.8.01": "Complementary angles sum to <math><mrow><mn>90<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, supplementary to <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and vertical angles are equal.", "III.8.02": "With parallel lines, corresponding and alternate angles are equal, and same-side interior angles sum to <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.03": "A triangle's angles sum to <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; an exterior angle equals the sum of the two opposite interior angles.", "III.8.04": "<math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, where <math><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is the perpendicular height, not the slanted side.", "III.8.05": "<math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><mi>b<\/mi><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.8.06": "<math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>⋅<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: the average of the parallel sides, times the height.", "III.8.07": "Split into pieces and add, or take a bigger shape and subtract the cut-outs.", "III.8.08": "The radius <math><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> runs from center to circle; the diameter is <math><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; a chord joins two points of the circle; an arc is a piece of it.", "III.8.09": "<math><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>π<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.8.10": "<math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>π<\/mi><msup><mi>r<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.8.11": "Surface area is the total area of all the faces: draw the net and add.", "III.8.12": "<math><mrow><mi>V<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: base area times height. For a box, <math><mrow><mi>V<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>l<\/mi><mi>w<\/mi><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.13": "<math><mrow><mi>V<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>π<\/mi><msup><mi>r<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: the circle's area times the height.", "III.8.14": "<math><mrow><msub><mi>V<\/mi><mtext>cone<\/mtext><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>3<\/mn><\/mfrac><mi>π<\/mi><msup><mi>r<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><msub><mi>V<\/mi><mtext>sphere<\/mtext><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>4<\/mn><mn>3<\/mn><\/mfrac><mi>π<\/mi><msup><mi>r<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.15": "In a right triangle, <math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><msup><mi>b<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>c<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>, where <math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is the hypotenuse.", "III.8.16": "With <math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> longest: <math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><msup><mi>b<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>c<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> means right, <math><mrow><mo>&gt;<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> means acute, <math><mrow><mo>&lt;<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> means obtuse.", "III.8.17": "<span class=\"dm\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msqrt><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/msqrt><\/mrow><\/math><\/span>", "III.8.18": "The space diagonal of an <math><mrow><mi>l<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>w<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> box is <math><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>l<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><msup><mi>w<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>+<\/mo><msup><mi>h<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/msqrt><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.19": "A translation by <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> sends <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>↦<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.20": "Across the <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>-axis: <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>↦<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>. Across the <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>-axis: <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>. Across <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.21": "About the origin: <math><mrow><mn>90<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> counterclockwise <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>↦<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> gives <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mn>270<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> gives <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.22": "A dilation centered at the origin with scale factor <math><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> sends <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>↦<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.8.23": "Congruent: one maps onto the other by rigid moves. Similar: rigid moves plus a dilation.", "III.5.01": "A variable is a letter that stands for a number: unknown, or free to change.", "III.5.02": "Sum <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, difference <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, product <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, quotient <math><mrow><mo>÷<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; “<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> less than <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>” is <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.5.03": "Substitute each value in brackets, then follow the order of operations.", "III.5.04": "Terms are separated by <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; a coefficient multiplies a variable; a constant stands alone.", "III.5.05": "Like terms have the same variables to the same powers; combine them by adding their coefficients.", "III.5.06": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.5.07": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>: pull out the greatest common factor of every term.", "III.5.08": "Expressions are equivalent when they have the same value for every value of the variable.", "III.5.09": "Distribute, then combine like terms.", "III.5.10": "Perimeter adds side lengths; area multiplies them. Write each with variables, then simplify.", "III.5.11": "Each term and factor of a model has a meaning, and rewriting can reveal it.", "III.5.12": "<math><mrow><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>⋅<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> but <math><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; only like powers combine.", "III.5.13": "If a pattern grows by <math><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> each step, its <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>th term is <math><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.5.14": "Tiles are named by area: <math><mrow><msup><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> (big square), <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> (strip), <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> (small square); the other colour is negative.", "III.5.15": "Follow the trick with a variable: if the <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>'s cancel, the answer doesn't depend on <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.01": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is the number in <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> put together.", "I.4.02": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is what's left when <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is taken from <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.03": "Story, then number sentence, then an answer with its unit.", "I.4.04": "Taking away, comparing and finding a missing part are all subtraction.", "I.4.05": "part + part = whole, and whole − part = the other part.", "I.4.06": "The bonds of 5: <math><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, and their turnarounds.", "I.4.07": "Partners of 10: <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>5<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.08": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and every double is even.", "I.4.09": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.10": "Split the second number to complete a ten: <math><mrow><mn>8<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>13<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.11": "Count on from the larger addend: <math><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>14<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>14<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.12": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.13": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: start at <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and count back <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> steps.", "I.4.14": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo>?<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> is the same as <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo>?<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.15": "Split the number you subtract: <math><mrow><mn>14<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>14<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.16": "If <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.17": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo>?<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> has answer <math><mrow><mo>?<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.18": "<math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> means “is the same amount as”, not “the answer is”.", "I.4.19": "Every fact up to <math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> follows from a few strategies: bonds, doubles and make ten.", "I.4.20": "<math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> because <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: recall subtraction through addition.", "I.4.21": "Add or subtract tens on the tens digit: <math><mrow><mn>30<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>40<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>70<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>45<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>30<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>15<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.4.22": "Add tens to tens and ones to ones; regroup 10 ones as a ten.", "I.4.23": "Subtract ones from ones and tens from tens; break a ten if the ones run short.", "III.4.01": "<math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> means <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> factors of <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> multiplied together.", "III.4.02": "<math><mrow><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> is 1 followed by <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> zeros; multiplying by <math><mrow><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> moves the decimal point <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> places right.", "III.4.03": "Exponents come before <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mo>÷<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, and act only on what they touch: <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><msup><mn>3<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.4.04": "<math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>m<\/mi><\/msup><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.4.05": "<math><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>m<\/mi><\/msup><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, for <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.4.06": "<math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>m<\/mi><\/msup><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2778em\"><\/mspace><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><msup><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2778em\"><\/mspace><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><msup><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.4.07": "<math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> for <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.4.08": "A number in scientific notation is <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>, with <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> an integer.", "III.4.09": "<math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>m<\/mi><\/msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>; to divide, divide and subtract exponents.", "III.4.10": "Compare the powers of ten first; if they match, compare the front numbers. To say how many times bigger, divide.", "III.4.11": "<math><mrow><msqrt><mi>x<\/mi><\/msqrt><\/mrow><\/math> is the non-negative number whose square is <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.4.12": "<math><mrow><mroot><mi>x<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/mroot><\/mrow><\/math> is the number whose cube is <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; negative numbers have negative cube roots.", "III.4.13": "If <math><mrow><msup><mi>a<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><msup><mi>b<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math>, then <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><msqrt><mi>x<\/mi><\/msqrt><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.4.14": "An irrational number is a real number that is not a ratio of two integers.", "III.4.15": "<math><mrow><mi>ℕ<\/mi><mo>⊂<\/mo><mi>ℤ<\/mi><mo>⊂<\/mo><mi>ℚ<\/mi><mo>⊂<\/mo><mi>ℝ<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; the irrationals are the reals outside <math><mrow><mi>ℚ<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.4.16": "Approximate each number to enough decimal places, or compare squares.", "III.4.17": "Linear growth adds the same amount each step; exponential growth multiplies by the same factor.", "I.3.01": "<math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> ones make <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> ten.", "I.3.02": "In a teen numeral, the 1 is one ten and the second digit counts the ones.", "I.3.03": "<math><mrow><mtext>number<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mtext>tens<\/mtext><mo>×<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mtext>ones<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>", "I.3.04": "A two-digit number with tens digit <math><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and ones digit <math><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is <math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.3.05": "1 ten = 10 ones, so a number has many tens-and-ones names.", "I.3.06": "10 tens = 1 hundred = 100 ones.", "I.3.07": "Value of a digit = digit × place value.", "I.3.08": "Expanded form writes a number as the sum of its digits' values: <math><mrow><mn>347<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>300<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>40<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.3.09": "Read the hundreds, then name the last two digits together.", "I.3.10": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>±<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> changes the tens digit by 1; <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>±<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> changes the hundreds digit by 1.", "I.3.11": "On the chart, right is <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, down is <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, and each column shares a ones digit.", "I.3.12": "Compare the number of digits, then compare digits from the left until they differ.", "II.6.01": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.6.02": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>−<\/mo><mfrac><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.6.03": "A fraction splits into same-denominator parts in many ways: <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>3<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>2<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.6.04": "Add or subtract the wholes and the fractions separately, regrouping <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>n<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> when needed.", "II.6.05": "A common denominator is a common multiple of the denominators; the smallest is their LCM.", "II.6.06": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, or rename over the LCM and add.", "II.6.07": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>−<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, or rename over the LCM and subtract.", "II.6.08": "Rename the fraction parts over a common denominator, then combine wholes and parts, regrouping if needed.", "II.6.09": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.6.10": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>×<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.6.11": "For <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>: <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>f<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> when <math><mrow><mi>f<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>f<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> when <math><mrow><mi>f<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.6.12": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.6.13": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.6.14": "Decide what each fraction describes, choose the operation, then check that the answer is reasonable.", "II.3.01": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is how many each of <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> groups gets when <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is shared equally.", "II.3.02": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> also counts how many groups of size <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> fit into <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.3.03": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo>?<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> means <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mo>?<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.3.04": "Every division fact up to <math><mrow><mn>100<\/mn><mo>÷<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> comes from a times fact up to <math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.3.05": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; for <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is undefined.", "II.3.06": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> with <math><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.3.07": "A remainder can be rounded up, dropped, or shared as a fraction: the question decides.", "II.3.08": "Divide the basic fact and keep track of the tens: <math><mrow><mn>240<\/mn><mo>÷<\/mo><mn>40<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>24<\/mn><mo>÷<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.3.09": "Divide the tens, trade any leftover tens for ones, then divide the ones.", "II.3.10": "Divide, multiply, subtract, bring down: repeat for each place.", "II.3.11": "Estimate each quotient digit by rounding the divisor, then adjust if the product is too big or too small.", "II.3.12": "2, 5, 10: last digit. 4: last two digits. 3, 9: digit sum. 6: tests for 2 and 3.", "II.3.13": "Divide when a total is split into equal groups and either the group size or the number of groups is missing.", "II.3.14": "Solve a two-step problem one step at a time, and write it as one equation with a box for the unknown.", "II.3.15": "Replace the numbers with nearby compatible numbers whose division is easy.", "II.8.01": "Brackets; then <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mo>÷<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> from left to right; then <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> from left to right.", "II.8.02": "Translate words into an expression, using brackets to show what must happen first.", "II.8.03": "Evaluate inside brackets first, then follow the order of operations, rewriting the expression after each step.", "II.8.04": "Find the rule from each term to the next, or from each term's position to the term.", "II.8.05": "A rule turns each input into exactly one output; undo the steps to go backwards.", "II.8.06": "Use the inverse operation: <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo>□<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> gives <math><mrow><mo>□<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mo>□<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> gives <math><mrow><mo>□<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.8.07": "Equivalent expressions have the same value: <math><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.8.08": "Write one expression for the whole problem, with brackets where the story groups things, then evaluate it.", "II.8.09": "An equation is a balance: doing the same to both sides keeps it true. <math><mrow><mo>□<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> gives <math><mrow><mo>□<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.01": "A ratio <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> says: for every <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> of one thing, there are <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> of another.", "III.2.02": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>a<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> for any nonzero number <math><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.03": "In a ratio table every row is a multiple of one row; you may scale rows and add rows.", "III.2.04": "A unit rate is an amount per one unit of something else.", "III.2.05": "Unit rate <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">/<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">/<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>⋅<\/mo><mfrac><mi>d<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.2.06": "The pairs of equivalent ratios lie on a straight line through the origin.", "III.2.07": "A proportion <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> says two ratios are equal; solve by scaling or cross products.", "III.2.08": "<math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is proportional to <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> when <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>y<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> is the same for every pair: <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.09": "In <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, the constant of proportionality <math><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>y<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> is the <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> for one <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.10": "Every length in a scale drawing is the real length times the same scale factor.", "III.2.11": "Multiply by a conversion factor equal to 1, like <math><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>100<\/mn><mtext> cm<\/mtext><\/mrow><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> m<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, so the old unit cancels.", "III.2.12": "To share <math><mrow><mi>T<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> in the ratio <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, one part is <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>T<\/mi><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.13": "<math><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, so <math><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>d<\/mi><mi>r<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>d<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.14": "Compare <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> with <math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo>:<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> by making one term the same, or by comparing <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> with <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.2.15": "If one amount goes up as the other goes down, with a fixed product, the relationship is inverse: <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.5.01": "Name a pattern with letters: red-blue-red-blue is AB, red-blue-blue is ABB.", "I.5.02": "A repeating pattern is a core repeated over and over.", "I.5.03": "A rule describes a pattern in words, and works with any items.", "I.5.04": "In a growing pattern each step changes by a rule, like “+3 each time”.", "I.5.05": "Find the step from the differences, then use it forward, backward or in a gap.", "I.5.06": "Sorting by one attribute puts every object in exactly one group.", "I.5.07": "Two overlapping circles sort by two attributes into four regions.", "I.5.08": "Even: <math><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>. Odd: <math><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>. The last digit tells which.", "I.5.09": "Compare two things attribute by attribute: shape, colour, size, number, position.", "I.5.10": "A statement is either true or false, and a false one can be corrected.", "I.5.11": "Always: true in every case. Sometimes: in some. Never: in none.", "I.5.12": "“If <math><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then <math><mrow><mi>Q<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>”: whenever <math><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is true, <math><mrow><mi>Q<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is true.", "I.5.13": "In a logic grid, each row and each column has exactly one yes.", "I.5.14": "If <math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>B<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mi>C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then <math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mi>C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: chain the clues.", "I.5.15": "Keep only the numbers that fit every clue.", "III.1.01": "A negative number measures the opposite direction from a chosen zero.", "III.1.02": "On a number line, further right means greater: <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mn>7<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.1.03": "<math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">|<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">|<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> is the distance from <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> to <math><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, so it is never negative.", "III.1.04": "Same signs: add the sizes, keep the sign. Different signs: subtract the sizes, keep the larger one's sign.", "III.1.05": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>: subtracting means adding the opposite.", "III.1.07": "Same signs: positive quotient. Different signs: negative quotient.", "III.1.08": "Brackets, then exponents, then <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mo>÷<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> left to right, then <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">+<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> left to right.", "III.1.09": "A rational number can be written <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, with <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> integers and <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.1.10": "Integer sign rules plus fraction rules: common denominator, then add signed numerators.", "III.1.11": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>⋅<\/mo><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, and dividing by <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> means multiplying by <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>d<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.1.12": "In lowest terms, <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> terminates exactly when <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> has no prime factors but 2 and 5.", "III.1.13": "Multiply by 10, 100, … to shift one block, subtract, and the endless tail cancels.", "III.1.14": "Put everything in one form, then compare; among negatives, the bigger size is the smaller number.", "III.1.15": "The axes cut the plane into quadrants I to IV, counterclockwise from top right.", "II.5.01": "A whole cut into <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> equal parts makes <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>ths: halves, thirds, fourths, sixths, eighths.", "II.5.02": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> is one of <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> equal parts; the bigger <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, the smaller the part.", "II.5.03": "In <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, the denominator <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> names the size of the parts, and the numerator <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> counts them.", "II.5.04": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> of <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: split <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> into <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> equal groups and take <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> of them, <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>×<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.5.05": "To place <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, split each unit into <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> equal jumps and count <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> jumps from 0.", "II.5.06": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>n<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>n<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.5.07": "Equivalent fractions name the same amount, and the same point on the number line.", "II.5.08": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> for any <math><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>; read backwards, it simplifies.", "II.5.09": "With equal denominators, compare numerators: <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mfrac><mi>b<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> exactly when <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.5.10": "With equal numerators, the smaller denominator gives the larger fraction.", "II.5.11": "Rename with a common denominator and compare numerators, or compare each fraction with a benchmark like <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.5.12": "<math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mfrac><mn>3<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>3<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>: a whole-number part, plus a fraction part less than 1.", "II.5.13": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> with <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is at least 1; divide to convert: if <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mi>q<\/mi><mfrac><mi>r<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.5.15": "A fraction is a size relative to a whole; compare fractions only with the same whole.", "I.1.01": "Counting matches each object with exactly one number word.", "I.1.02": "Each number word comes right after exactly one other, in a fixed list.", "I.1.03": "A teen number is <math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> plus some ones: <math><mrow><mn>13<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, up to <math><mrow><mn>20<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.1.04": "Decades: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50. Inside each, the ones run 1 to 9.", "I.1.05": "After <math><mrow><mn>100<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, the old pattern repeats: <math><mrow><mn>101<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>102<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>110<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>120<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.1.06": "The digits are <math><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> to <math><mrow><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>; numbers from <math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> to <math><mrow><mn>20<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> use two digits.", "I.1.07": "The last number word counted is the total.", "I.1.09": "Subitizing: knowing how many at a glance, up to about 4 or 5.", "I.1.10": "Group into fives and tens: <math><mrow><mn>8<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mn>9<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.1.11": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: start at <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and say <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> more numbers.", "I.1.12": "Counting back <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> steps from <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> lands on <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.1.13": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is the next number; <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is the one before.", "I.1.14": "Counting by 10s adds 1 to the tens digit each time.", "I.1.15": "Counting by 5s: the last digit goes 5, 0, 5, 0…", "I.1.16": "Counting by 2s from 0 lists the even numbers: <math><mrow><mn>2<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.9.01": "<math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> cm<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mtext> mm<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> m<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mtext> cm<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> km<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1000<\/mn><mtext> m<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.02": "<math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> ft<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><mtext> in<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> yd<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mtext> ft<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> mi<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5280<\/mn><mtext> ft<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1760<\/mn><mtext> yd<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.03": "<math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> kg<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1000<\/mn><mtext> g<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> lb<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>16<\/mn><mtext> oz<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> kg<\/mtext><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>2.2<\/mn><mtext> lb<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.04": "<math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> L<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1000<\/mn><mtext> mL<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>. US: <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> gal<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mtext> qt<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> qt<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mtext> pt<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> pt<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mtext> cups<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.05": "<math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> min<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mtext> s<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> h<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mtext> min<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mtext> day<\/mtext><mo>=<\/mo><mn>24<\/mn><mtext> h<\/mtext><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.06": "Perimeter is the sum of the side lengths; for a rectangle, <math><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>l<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>w<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.07": "Area counts the unit squares that cover a shape with no gaps or overlaps, in units like cm² and m².", "II.9.08": "<math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>l<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>w<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.9.09": "Equal perimeters can have different areas, and equal areas can have different perimeters.", "II.9.10": "Volume counts the unit cubes that fill a solid, in units like cm³ and m³.", "II.9.11": "<math><mrow><mi>V<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>l<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>w<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, where <math><mrow><mi>B<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is the area of the base.", "II.9.12": "A segment has two endpoints, a ray one, a line none. Parallel lines never meet; perpendicular lines meet at right angles.", "II.9.13": "Right: <math><mrow><mn>90<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>. Acute: less than <math><mrow><mn>90<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>. Obtuse: between <math><mrow><mn>90<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>. Straight: <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.14": "Centre on the vertex, put 0 on one arm, and read the scale that starts from 0 on that arm.", "II.9.15": "Angles side by side add; on a straight line they sum to <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and around a point to <math><mrow><mn>360<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.16": "By sides: equilateral, isosceles, scalene. By angles: acute, right, obtuse. The angles add to <math><mrow><mn>180<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.17": "Parallelogram: two pairs of parallel sides. Rectangle: four right angles. Rhombus: four equal sides. Square: both.", "II.9.18": "A line of symmetry reflects a shape exactly onto itself.", "II.9.19": "The point <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> is <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> units right and <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> units up from the origin <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.9.20": "Convert to common units first, choose length, area or volume, then compute and label the answer.", "I.7.01": "Compare lengths by lining up one end; use a third object when you can't bring them together.", "I.7.02": "Length = the number of equal units that fit end to end, with no gaps or overlaps.", "I.7.03": "Line up 0 with one end; read the mark at the other end.", "I.7.04": "Lengths add and subtract like numbers, when the units match.", "I.7.05": "On a balance, heavier sinks and equal weights stay level.", "I.7.06": "Compare capacity by filling with one unit and counting.", "I.7.07": "On the hour, the minute hand points to 12 and the hour hand points to the hour.", "I.7.08": "Half past is 30 minutes after the hour: minute hand on 6, hour hand halfway to the next number.", "I.7.09": "Minutes past the hour = the minute hand's number × 5.", "I.7.10": "A calendar shows a month in weeks of 7 days: one column, one weekday.", "I.7.11": "Count mixed coins from the biggest value down, counting on as you go.", "I.7.12": "Change = amount paid − price. Find it by counting up from the price.", "I.7.13": "Tally marks record counts in groups of five, so totals can be counted by 5s.", "I.7.14": "In a picture graph, each symbol stands for one item, or for a number set by the key.", "I.7.15": "A bar's length shows a count, read on a scale that starts at 0.", "I.7.16": "Data work has four steps: ask a question, collect, organize, interpret.", "II.4.01": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> and <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> are a factor pair of <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> when <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.4.02": "The multiples of <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> are <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>…<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is a multiple of <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> exactly when <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is a factor of <math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.4.03": "A prime has exactly two factors, 1 and itself; a composite has more than two.", "II.4.04": "Circle the next number not crossed out, cross out its multiples, repeat; up to 100, stopping after 7 is enough.", "II.4.05": "Every whole number above 1 is a product of primes in exactly one way, apart from order.", "II.4.06": "The greatest common factor is the largest number that divides both: <math><mrow><mi>gcd<\/mi><mo>&#x2061;<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>18<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.4.07": "Dividing by the GCF puts a fraction in simplest form at once, and factors a sum: <math><mrow><mn>12<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>18<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.4.08": "The least common multiple is the smallest positive number that both divide: <math><mrow><mi>lcm<\/mi><mo>&#x2061;<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.4.09": "The LCM of the denominators is the least common denominator, and <math><mrow><mi>gcd<\/mi><mo>&#x2061;<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>×<\/mo><mi>lcm<\/mi><mo>&#x2061;<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.4.10": "<math><mrow><msup><mi>n<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, …, 144.", "II.4.11": "Same parity: sum and difference are even. Mixed: odd. A product is odd only when every factor is odd.", "II.4.12": "A perfect number is the sum of its factors other than itself: <math><mrow><mn>6<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.7.01": "A rule turns each input <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> into one output <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; write it as an equation, like <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.7.02": "Plot each pair <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> as a point: across <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then up <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.7.03": "Rate of change <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>change in <\/mtext><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mtext>change in <\/mtext><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>, in units of <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> per unit of <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.7.04": "<math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mtext>rise<\/mtext><mtext>run<\/mtext><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.7.05": "Any two slope triangles on one line are similar, so rise ÷ run is the same everywhere.", "III.7.06": "<math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: slope <math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>-intercept <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.7.07": "<math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is proportional; <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> with <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is linear but not proportional.", "III.7.08": "Linear: equal steps in <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> give equal changes in <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>. Anything else is nonlinear.", "III.7.09": "A function assigns each input exactly one output.", "III.7.10": "Compare rates (slopes) and starting values (intercepts), whatever form each function comes in.", "III.7.11": "Rising means increasing, falling means decreasing, flat means no change; steeper means faster.", "III.7.12": "In a model <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is the rate per unit and <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> the starting value.", "I.6.01": "Polygons are named by their sides: triangle 3, quadrilateral 4, pentagon 5, hexagon 6.", "I.6.02": "A polygon has straight sides and corners (vertices); a circle has one curved edge and none.", "I.6.03": "A shape's name depends on its properties, not on how it is turned or where it sits.", "I.6.04": "Solids: cube, rectangular prism, sphere, cylinder, cone, pyramid.", "I.6.05": "A cube has 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 vertices.", "I.6.06": "Compose shapes by fitting smaller ones together, with no gaps or overlaps.", "I.6.07": "Decompose a shape by cutting it into smaller shapes that fit back exactly.", "I.6.08": "Count cubes layer by layer: a box shape has rows × columns × layers.", "I.6.09": "Position words describe where one object is relative to another.", "I.6.10": "A route is a list of moves: forward or back some squares, and quarter turns left or right.", "I.6.11": "A half is one of 2 equal parts: <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.6.12": "A quarter (a fourth) is one of 4 equal parts: <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>4<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> is half of <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "I.6.13": "A line of symmetry splits a shape into two mirror-image halves.", "I.6.14": "Each clue is a property; the answer must have all of them.", "II.7.01": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>10<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>3<\/mn><mn>10<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>: the first place after the point counts tenths.", "II.7.02": "<math><mrow><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.01<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>: the second place after the point counts hundredths.", "II.7.03": "<math><mrow><mn>3.472<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>4<\/mn><mn>10<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>7<\/mn><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mn>2<\/mn><mn>1000<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "II.7.04": "Rename a fraction with denominator 10, 100 or 1000 to write it as a decimal, or divide top by bottom.", "II.7.05": "Compare decimals place by place from the left, after adding zeros to make them the same length.", "II.7.06": "Look one place right of the rounding place: 5 or more rounds up, 4 or less rounds down.", "II.7.07": "Line up the decimal points, fill empty places with zeros, and add as with whole numbers.", "II.7.08": "Line up the points, fill empty places with zeros, and subtract as with whole numbers, regrouping as needed.", "II.7.09": "<math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> moves every digit <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> places left; <math><mrow><mo>÷<\/mo><msup><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> moves every digit <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> places right.", "II.7.10": "Multiply as if there were no point, then give the answer as many decimal places as the decimal had.", "II.7.11": "Multiply as whole numbers; the product has as many decimal places as the two factors together.", "II.7.12": "Divide as usual, putting the point in the quotient directly above the point in the dividend.", "II.7.13": "Move the point in the divisor and the dividend the same number of places, until the divisor is whole.", "II.7.14": "Money is a decimal with two places: whole units, and hundredths called cents.", "II.2.01": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> means <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> equal groups of <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> added to itself <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> times.", "II.2.02": "An array of <math><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> rows and <math><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> columns holds <math><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> objects.", "II.2.03": "<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is half of <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.2.04": "<math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is doubling twice; <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mn>6<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> is <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> plus one more group, or double the <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.2.05": "<math><mrow><mn>9<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>; <math><mrow><mn>8<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is double, double, double; <math><mrow><mn>7<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.2.06": "The table is symmetric, <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, so 55 facts cover all 100.", "II.2.07": "Area of a rectangle = length × width, and splitting it shows <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.2.08": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>, and <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.2.09": "Multiply the non-zero parts, then attach all the zeros: <math><mrow><mn>30<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mn>400<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>12<\/mn><mo>×<\/mo><mn>1000<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.2.10": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mi>t<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: two partial products.", "II.2.11": "Multiply each digit by the one-digit factor, right to left, adding each carry to the next product.", "II.2.12": "<math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mi>a<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mi>c<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> has four partial products: tens × tens, tens × ones, ones × tens, ones × ones.", "II.2.13": "Multiply the top number by each digit below, shift each row to that digit's place, and add the rows.", "II.2.14": "Multiply when the story has equal groups, an array, or \"<math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> times as many\".", "II.2.15": "A product is odd only when every factor is odd; doubling one factor and halving the other keeps the product.", "I.1.08": "Adding <math><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><\/math> changes nothing: <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "II.5.14": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>b<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.1.06": "Same signs: positive. Different signs: negative.", "I.2.01": "Match one to one: the leftovers show which set has more, and how many more.", "I.2.02": "Two groups are equal when they have the same number of objects, however they are arranged.", "I.2.03": "On a number line, each number sits its own number of steps from 0.", "I.2.04": "Of two numbers, the one farther right on the number line is greater.", "I.2.05": "On a 0–20 line, <math><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> sits <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> steps past 10.", "I.2.06": "Ascending order is least to greatest; descending is greatest to least.", "I.2.07": "Cardinal numbers say how many; ordinal numbers say which position.", "I.2.08": "Compare tens first, then ones: 16 is more than 11.", "I.2.09": "Compare the tens; if the tens are equal, compare the ones.", "I.2.10": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: equal. <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is greater. <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is less.", "I.2.11": "Estimate by comparing with a known amount, then check by counting.", "I.2.12": "The difference <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> tells how many more <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is than <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.01": "<math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>p<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.3.02": "Fraction to decimal: divide. Decimal to percent: multiply by 100. Percent to decimal: divide by 100.", "III.3.03": "<math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> of <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>p<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><mo>⋅<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.04": "If <math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> of <math><mrow><mi>W<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then <math><mrow><mi>W<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><mo>÷<\/mo><mfrac><mi>p<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.05": "<math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> is <math><mrow><mfrac><mi>a<\/mi><mi>W<\/mi><\/mfrac><mo>×<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> of <math><mrow><mi>W<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.06": "Over 100% means more than the whole; under 1% means less than one hundredth.", "III.3.07": "A rise of <math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> multiplies by <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mi>p<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>; percent increase <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>new<\/mtext><mo>−<\/mo><mtext>old<\/mtext><\/mrow><mtext>old<\/mtext><\/mfrac><mo>×<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.08": "A drop of <math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> multiplies by <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mfrac><mi>p<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>; percent decrease <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>old<\/mtext><mo>−<\/mo><mtext>new<\/mtext><\/mrow><mtext>old<\/mtext><\/mfrac><mo>×<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.09": "Sale price <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> original price <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"><\/mspace><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mtext>discount<\/mtext><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.10": "Total <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> price <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"><\/mspace><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mtext>tax rate<\/mtext><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; a tip is a percent of the bill.", "III.3.11": "Markup <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>price<\/mtext><mo>−<\/mo><mtext>cost<\/mtext><\/mrow><mtext>cost<\/mtext><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>; profit margin <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>price<\/mtext><mo>−<\/mo><mtext>cost<\/mtext><\/mrow><mtext>price<\/mtext><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.12": "<math><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>P<\/mi><mi>r<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, and the total amount is <math><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>P<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>P<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.13": "Percent error <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">|<\/mo><mtext>measured<\/mtext><mo>−<\/mo><mtext>actual<\/mtext><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">|<\/mo><\/mrow><mtext>actual<\/mtext><\/mfrac><mo>×<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.3.14": "Up <math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> then down <math><mrow><mi>p<\/mi><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> leaves <math><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mfrac><mi>p<\/mi><mn>100<\/mn><\/mfrac><msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/math> of the start.", "III.3.15": "Percent of a total <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mtext>count<\/mtext><mtext>total<\/mtext><\/mfrac><mo>×<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mo>%<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; its pie slice is that share of <math><mrow><mn>360<\/mn><mi>°<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.3.16": "Round the base, use a benchmark percent, then check the answer makes sense.", "III.3.17": "Chain the multipliers: each percent change is one factor, applied to the current amount.", "III.6.01": "An equation says two expressions are equal; a solution is a value that makes it true.", "III.6.02": "Undo adding by subtracting, and subtracting by adding, on both sides.", "III.6.03": "Undo multiplying by dividing both sides; for a fractional coefficient, multiply by its reciprocal.", "III.6.04": "For <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>: subtract <math><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>, then divide by <math><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.6.05": "Distribute, combine like terms, then solve the two-step equation.", "III.6.06": "Collect the variable on one side and the numbers on the other.", "III.6.07": "Define the variable, write the equation, solve, and answer in words with units.", "III.6.08": "<math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> means less than; <math><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> means less than or equal. The solutions fill an interval.", "III.6.09": "Solve like an equation, but multiplying or dividing by a negative flips the sign.", "III.6.10": "Undo the adding, then the multiplying; flip the sign when you divide by a negative.", "III.6.11": "To make a variable the subject, undo everything around it, just as in solving.", "III.6.12": "Look before you leap: undo operations, balance both sides, or clear fractions, and always check.", "III.9.01": "A statistical question expects variability in its answers.", "III.9.02": "<math><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">¯<\/mo><\/mover><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>⋯<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>n<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.9.03": "Order the data. Odd count: the middle value. Even count: the mean of the two middle values.", "III.9.04": "Range <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> maximum <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0.05em\">−<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> minimum.", "III.9.05": "<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R<\/mi><\/mrow><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>Q<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>Q<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><\/math>: the spread of the middle half.", "III.9.06": "Five-number summary: minimum, <math><mrow><msub><mi>Q<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><\/math>, median, <math><mrow><msub><mi>Q<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msub><\/mrow><\/math>, maximum.", "III.9.07": "Read a dot plot for centre, spread and shape: clusters, gaps, peaks and outliers.", "III.9.08": "A histogram groups numbers into equal-width bins; each bar's height is the count in its bin.", "III.9.09": "<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D<\/mi><\/mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mo largeop=\"true\" data-big=\"1\">∑<\/mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">|<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">¯<\/mo><\/mover><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">|<\/mo><\/mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.9.10": "A sample is part of the population; in a random sample, everyone has the same chance of being chosen.", "III.9.11": "Sample proportion <math><mrow><mo>×<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math> population size estimates the count in the population.", "III.9.12": "Compare centres and spreads, then measure the gap between centres in units of spread.", "III.9.13": "<math><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>A<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mtext>favorable outcomes<\/mtext><mtext>total outcomes<\/mtext><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math> when all outcomes are equally likely.", "III.9.14": "Experimental probability <math><mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mtext>times it happened<\/mtext><mtext>number of trials<\/mtext><\/mfrac><\/mrow><\/math>", "III.9.15": "Counting principle: <math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> choices followed by <math><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> choices give <math><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>×<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> outcomes.", "III.9.16": "Independent events: <math><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>A<\/mi><mtext> and <\/mtext><mi>B<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>P<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>A<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><mo>×<\/mo><mi>P<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>B<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>.", "III.9.17": "A simulation copies each chance event with a random device that has the same probability.", "III.9.18": "A scatter plot shows pairs <math><mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">(<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/math>; the pattern shows how the two variables are related.", "III.9.19": "Fit a line <math><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/math> by eye, then use it to predict.", "III.9.20": "A two-way table counts data by two categories; divide by row or column totals to compare."};
